module gud-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6-guam }

// The District Court of Guam's own periods, computed under the federal
// rules (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). Each period applies "unless
// otherwise ordered" where the rule says so. Rules that state no period or
// limit stay out: non-filing of discovery (CVLR 5), sanctions (CVLR 11),
// amended pleadings (CVLR 15), class action captions (CVLR 23),
// interrogatory and admission formats (CVLR 33, 36), entry of judgments
// (CVLR 58-1), injunctions, bonds and receivers (CVLR 65, 65.1, 66),
// magistrate judge duties (CVLR 72) and the clerk's authority (CVLR 77).
// Periods the rules state in units lit/core does not count stay in notes:
// exhibit copies three business days before an evidentiary hearing (CVLR
// 7(k)(4)), notice of a jury case's settlement at least 24 hours before
// the date set (CVLR 54(a)), and the scheduling conference "approximately
// ninety (90) days" after the complaint (CVLR 16-1(b)(1)). The negotiated
// extension caps of CVLR 7(g) (14 days for an opposition, 7 for a reply,
// one extension per motion) bound an extension, not a filing. The earlier
// D. Guam outline's FRCP flow and its Supreme Court decisions (Twombly,
// Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby, Reeves, Catlin, Bowles,
// Hamer) are FRCP and FRAP authority and belong to lit/frcp and lit/frap;
// its Ninth Circuit decisions (Eitel v. McCool; Lopez v. Smith) are
// removed: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A brief or memorandum supporting or responding to any motion: at most
/// 25 pages unless otherwise ordered, exclusive of the case caption, tables,
/// exhibits, declarations and certificates (CVLR 7(c)).
limit motion-memorandum { pages <= 25 cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(c)" } cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(c)"
/// A reply memorandum: at most 15 pages (CVLR 7(c)).
limit reply-memorandum { pages <= 15 cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(c)" } cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(c)"
/// An ex parte motion to exceed the page limits: no more than two pages,
/// requesting a specific number of additional pages (CVLR 7(d)(2)).
limit page-limit-motion { pages <= 2 cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(d)" } cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(d)"
/// A trial brief: at most 25 pages without leave of court (CVLR 16-1(e)).
limit trial-brief { pages <= 25 cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(e)" } cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(e)"
/// A letter brief seeking expedited discovery assistance: five pages or
/// less, inclusive of all exhibits, unless otherwise ordered (CVLR
/// 37(c)(2)).
limit discovery-letter-brief { pages <= 5 cite "D. Guam CVLR 37(c)" } cite "D. Guam CVLR 37(c)"

/// A concise statement supporting or opposing summary judgment: no longer
/// than five pages, unless it contains no more than 1500 words (CVLR
/// 56(e)).
limit concise-statement {
  pages <= 5 cite "D. Guam CVLR 56(e)"
  words <= 1_500 cite "D. Guam CVLR 56(e)"
} cite "D. Guam CVLR 56(e)"

/// A motion is filed (CVLR 7(f)).
event MotionFiled() paper motion-memorandum
/// An opposition to a motion is filed; with several oppositions, the last
/// one (CVLR 7(f)).
event OppositionFiled() paper motion-memorandum
/// A reply memorandum is filed (CVLR 7(f)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-memorandum
/// A motion to exceed the page limits is filed (CVLR 7(d)).
event PageLimitMotionFiled() paper page-limit-motion
/// The last day a reply brief would be due passes (CVLR 7(i)).
event ReplyDueDatePassed()
/// An evidentiary hearing on a motion is held (CVLR 7(k)).
event EvidentiaryHearingHeld()
/// The ruling or order sought to be reconsidered is filed (CVLR 7(p)(2)).
event RulingFiled()
/// The court rules that a motion to dismiss or for judgment on the
/// pleadings will be treated as one for summary judgment (CVLR 12).
event ConvertedToSummaryJudgment()
/// The complaint is filed (CVLR 16-1(b)(1), 26(f)(1)).
event ComplaintFiled()
/// The scheduling conference set by the court is held (CVLR 26(f)(1)).
event SchedulingConferenceHeld()
/// An objection to pretrial disclosures under FRCP 26(a)(3) is filed (CVLR
/// 16-1(d)).
event PretrialDisclosureObjectionFiled()
/// Trial commences on the date set (CVLR 16-1(c), (e)-(i), 51).
event TrialBegins()
/// A trial brief is filed and served (CVLR 16-1(e)).
event TrialBriefFiled() paper trial-brief
/// A mediation concludes (CVLR 16-2(b)(2)(F)).
event MediationConcluded()
/// A letter brief for expedited discovery assistance is filed (CVLR
/// 37(c)(2)).
event DiscoveryLetterBriefFiled() paper discovery-letter-brief
/// Judgment is entered, or an order denying a motion under FRCP 50(b),
/// 52(b) or 59, or an order remanding a removed action (CVLR 54(b)(2)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A bill of costs is filed (CVLR 54(b)(4)).
event BillOfCostsFiled()
/// The clerk taxes costs (CVLR 54(b)(5)).
event CostsTaxed()
/// The statement of consultation on a motion for attorney's fees is served
/// (CVLR 54(c)(4)).
event FeeConsultationStatementServed()
/// The responsive memorandum on a motion for attorney's fees is served
/// (CVLR 54(c)(4)).
event FeeResponseServed()
/// The court announces a decision awarding a judgment or order that
/// requires settlement and approval as to form (CVLR 58-2(a)).
event DecisionAnnounced()
/// The prevailing party serves its proposed draft judgment or order (CVLR
/// 58-2(a)).
event DraftJudgmentServed()
/// A party added after a consent reference to the magistrate judge appears
/// (CVLR 73(b)).
event AddedPartyAppeared()
/// Final judgment has been entered and the time for a new trial or
/// rehearing motion and for appeal has passed (CVLR 79(b)).
event ExhibitWithdrawalAvailable()
/// Written notice of withdrawal of an exhibit or deposition is given to all
/// parties (CVLR 79(b)).
event ExhibitWithdrawalNoticeGiven()

/// CVLR 7(f): unless otherwise ordered or provided by statute or rule, an
/// opposition is served and filed within 21 days of the filing of the
/// motion.
deadline opposition-period: 21.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(f)"
/// CVLR 7(f): a reply, if any, is served and filed within 14 days of the
/// filing of the opposition; with multiple oppositions, no later than 14
/// days after the last one is filed.
deadline reply-period: 14.days after OppositionFiled() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(f)"
/// CVLR 7(i): a party desiring oral argument files a request no later than
/// 7 days following the last day a reply brief would be due.
deadline oral-argument-request-period: 7.days after ReplyDueDatePassed() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(i)"
/// CVLR 7(k)(3): unless otherwise ordered, not less than 7 days before the
/// evidentiary hearing, each party who intends to present testimony files
/// and serves a witness list with summaries and time estimates.
deadline hearing-witness-list-period: 7.days before EvidentiaryHearingHeld() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(k)"
/// CVLR 7(k)(4): a party intending to use evidence not already of record
/// files an exhibit list not less than 7 days before the evidentiary
/// hearing; copies follow no later than three business days before it.
deadline hearing-exhibit-list-period: 7.days before EvidentiaryHearingHeld() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(k)"
/// CVLR 7(p)(2): a motion for reconsideration is filed no later than 14
/// days after the filing of the ruling or order sought to be reconsidered.
deadline reconsideration-period: 14.days after RulingFiled() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 7(p)"
/// CVLR 12: when a motion to dismiss or for judgment on the pleadings
/// against a pro se party is treated as one for summary judgment and the
/// movant has not served the notice, the movant serves and files the
/// amended form notice within fourteen days of the court's ruling.
deadline pro-se-notice-period: 14.days after ConvertedToSummaryJudgment() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 12"
/// CVLR 16-1(b)(1): the Clerk issues the Scheduling Notice no later than 40
/// days after the complaint has been filed.
deadline scheduling-notice-period: 40.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(b)"
/// CVLR 26(f)(1): the parties confer under FRCP 26(f) and file the
/// Scheduling and Planning Conference Report within 75 days of the filing
/// of the complaint.
deadline planning-report-period: 75.days after ComplaintFiled() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 26(f)"
/// CVLR 26(f)(1): unless otherwise ordered, the FRCP 26(f) conference is
/// held no later than 21 days before any scheduling conference the court
/// sets.
deadline planning-conference-period: 21.days before SchedulingConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 26(f)"
/// CVLR 16-1(c): the parties have a final pretrial conference with the
/// assigned judge 7 days prior to trial.
deadline final-pretrial-conference-period: 7.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(c)"
/// CVLR 16-1(d): responses to objections to FRCP 26(a)(3) pretrial
/// disclosures are filed and served within 7 days of the filing of the
/// objection, unless leave shortens the time.
deadline disclosure-objection-response-period: 7.days after PretrialDisclosureObjectionFiled() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(d)"
/// CVLR 16-1(e): each party serves and files a trial brief, of at most 25
/// pages without leave, 30 days prior to the trial date.
deadline trial-brief-period: 30.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(e)"
/// CVLR 16-1(f)(1): fourteen days prior to trial, each party serves and
/// files its witness list.
deadline witness-list-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(f)"
/// CVLR 16-1(f)(2): fourteen days prior to trial, each party serves and
/// files its deposition, interrogatory and admission designations.
deadline discovery-designation-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(f)"
/// CVLR 16-1(f)(3): fourteen days prior to trial, each party serves and
/// files its exhibit list.
deadline exhibit-list-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(f)"
/// CVLR 16-1(g): fourteen days prior to trial, the plaintiff serves and
/// lodges a proposed Pretrial Order signed by each party.
deadline pretrial-order-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(g)"
/// CVLR 16-1(h), 51: in jury cases, unless otherwise ordered, proposed jury
/// instructions and verdict forms are served and filed not less than 14
/// days prior to the date trial is scheduled to commence.
deadline jury-instructions-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(h)"
/// CVLR 16-1(i)(2): in a case approved for waiver of pretrial preparation,
/// the attorneys meet 30 days before the date set for trial.
deadline waiver-meeting-period: 30.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(i)"
/// CVLR 16-1(i)(2): in a case approved for waiver of pretrial preparation,
/// each party files its statement of issues, witness and exhibit lists,
/// deposition designations and trial brief not less than 14 days before
/// the date set for trial.
deadline waiver-filings-period: 14.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-1(i)"
/// CVLR 16-2(b)(2)(F): within five days of the conclusion of a mediation,
/// the mediator files a report with the ADR Coordinator.
deadline mediator-report-period: 5.days after MediationConcluded() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 16-2(b)"
/// CVLR 54(b)(2): unless otherwise ordered, a bill of costs is filed and
/// served within 30 days of the entry of judgment, of an order denying a
/// motion under FRCP 50(b), 52(b) or 59, or of an order remanding a removed
/// action; noncompliance waives costs.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 54(b)"
/// CVLR 54(b)(4): within 14 days after a bill of costs is filed, the party
/// against whom costs are claimed files and serves specific objections.
deadline costs-objection-period: 14.days after BillOfCostsFiled() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 54(b)"
/// CVLR 54(b)(5): taxation of costs is reviewed on a motion filed and
/// served within 7 days after taxation by the clerk.
deadline costs-review-period: 7.days after CostsTaxed() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 54(b)"
/// CVLR 54(c)(4): unless otherwise ordered, an opposing party may file a
/// responsive memorandum within 14 days after service of the statement of
/// consultation.
deadline fee-response-period: 14.days after FeeConsultationStatementServed() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 54(c)"
/// CVLR 54(c)(4): unless otherwise ordered, the moving party may file a
/// reply memorandum within 7 days after service of the responsive
/// memorandum.
deadline fee-reply-period: 7.days after FeeResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 54(c)"
/// CVLR 58-2(a): except as otherwise ordered, within 7 days after the
/// announcement of a decision requiring settlement as to form, the
/// prevailing party prepares and serves a draft judgment or order.
deadline draft-judgment-period: 7.days after DecisionAnnounced() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 58-2(a)"
/// CVLR 58-2(a): a party receiving the proposed draft serves and files any
/// objection and a substitute draft within 7 days thereafter.
deadline draft-objection-period: 7.days after DraftJudgmentServed() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 58-2(a)"
/// CVLR 73(b): a party added after reference to the magistrate judge on
/// consent who chooses to consent files the notice within 21 days of its
/// appearance.
deadline added-party-consent-period: 21.days after AddedPartyAppeared() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 73(b)"
/// CVLR 79(b): after final judgment and the time for new trial, rehearing
/// and appeal, a party may withdraw its exhibit or deposition without
/// order upon 14 days written notice to all parties, unless another files
/// a notice of claim within that time.
deadline exhibit-claim-period: 14.days after ExhibitWithdrawalNoticeGiven() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 79(b)"
/// CVLR 79(c): exhibits and deposition transcripts not withdrawn within 40
/// days after the time notice may first be given under CVLR 79(b) may be
/// destroyed or otherwise disposed of by the clerk.
deadline unclaimed-exhibit-period: 40.days after ExhibitWithdrawalAvailable() counted_by frcp6-guam cite "D. Guam CVLR 79(c)"
